title: The solution is easy!
pid: fe2e24f1-7b2e-4319-af8a-f688ff9e7e55
body: |2-
  Writing essays is hard, and reading them can be tedious if the author guesses wrong about what the reader will want to know when. Webs of thought suffer neither problem.

  Recording relationships between ideas -- building the web -- is so easy that you don't even need to use complete sentences. Connecting phrases with arrows (e.g. "forgiveness -> freedom", "hope -> ambition", "self-confidence -> spiritual healing", ..) is enough to convey interesting information about how one sees the world. Collecting such relationships, it does not take much time at all to build a web that's fun to navigate (i.e. to look at, think about, meditate on).
